WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:04.960
Searching through the review aggregator site
Metacritic, you’ll find reviews for thousands

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:05.980
of games.

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:10.190
But there are thirty-one games that stand
alone, with rankings head and shoulders above

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:11.200
the rest.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:14.679
These are the only near-perfect games out
there, according to the rankings on Metacritic.

00:00:15.889 --> 00:00:20.130
It should surprise no one that Rockstar is
going to be a part of any conversation involving

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.050
the greatest games of all time.

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:26.450
The Grand Theft Auto Double Pack is a bit
of a cheat since it's two games, but it makes

00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:27.450
sense.

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:30.960
Collect two already great games into one package,
and you’ll make magic happen.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:35.750
The content in this rerelease of Grand Theft
Auto 3 and Grand Theft Auto: Vice City was

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:40.001
nothing new, but the graphics were given a
serious once-over to be at their absolute

00:00:40.001 --> 00:00:41.330
best for the era.

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:45.660
Many of the reviews are no longer available,
but reading the critic review quotes on Metacritic

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:48.240
is eye-opening for the joys of yesteryear.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:52.820
One reviewer wrote that ensuring you had 480p
television capabilities would make for the

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:55.360
"prettiest GTA experience you'll get on a
console."

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:56.880
Ah, 2003.

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:01.930
At the time, this was the cleanest and most
stable version of both these games available.

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:05.940
It isn't surprising that having the best versions
of these two already great games rolled into

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:08.130
one release was something to get excited about.

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:12.501
One of the great gaming bait-and-switches
of all time made for one of the PS2's most

00:01:12.501 --> 00:01:13.880
memorable games.

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:18.220
Metal Gear Solid 2: Sons of Liberty ticked
a lot of people off when it launched, as Metal

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:22.270
Gear Solid fans had no idea they would not
be playing as the grizzled protagonist Solid

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:24.400
Snake for most of the mission.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:28.850
Even though the game got a lot of love, new
protagonist Raiden received a lot of ire from

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:29.850
fans.

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:32.220
Though he's earned back a lot of goodwill
in the time since.

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:36.360
Metal Gear Solid 2 took the exciting stealth
gameplay of the original and cranked it up

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:37.360
with the power of the PS2.

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:41.960
The technological achievements of the game
were completely amazing, with some websites

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:45.890
calling it "something that looks as close
to real life as it gets on your TV."

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:50.470
This was also the entry in the series where
Hideo Kojima really got to flex his storytelling

00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:52.710
muscles to create a memorable narrative.

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:57.350
Gran Turismo is one of the oldest games on
this list; it was released for the original

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.710
PlayStation back in 1998.

00:01:59.710 --> 00:02:04.400
The battle between the disc-based PlayStation
and the cartridge-based Nintendo 64 was in

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:09.640
full swing, and Gran Turismo helped showcase
something that the N64 couldn't do: Total

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:10.640
realism.

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:14.650
Gran Turismo was like a glimpse into the future,
as you could seemingly design every element

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:18.299
of your car and take it through photo-realistic
races.

00:02:18.299 --> 00:02:23.349
Reviews lauded the game's customization, attention
to detail, and multiple ways to race.

00:02:23.349 --> 00:02:27.060
About the only knock on the original Gran
Turismo was the licensing aspect.

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:31.329
The game tasked players with earning licenses
by completing difficult driving tasks before

00:02:31.329 --> 00:02:33.560
entering higher-level races.

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:37.269
Considering how badly you'd lose a race if
you couldn't pass these tests, it's a rather

00:02:37.269 --> 00:02:38.269
small knock.

00:02:39.269 --> 00:02:40.659
You knew Link was going to show up on here.

00:02:40.659 --> 00:02:45.150
The Legend of Zelda: The Wind Waker is probably
one of the lesser-played titles in the series,

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:47.980
simply because it was originally released
on the GameCube.

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:52.499
It still featured the same great combination
of combat, puzzles, and exploration that the

00:02:52.499 --> 00:02:54.670
Legend of Zelda series is known for, however.

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:59.120
It also boasted one of the most striking visual
styles the series has ever adopted.

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:03.480
The Wind Waker utilized a cel-shaded graphic
style to appear as if it were a cartoon come

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:08.530
to life, but the game used its exaggerated
visuals to tell a deep and emotional story.

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:12.549
It also made great use of its beautiful art
direction with its sailing sections, where

00:03:12.549 --> 00:03:15.409
Link would hop on a boat and traverse between
islands.

00:03:15.409 --> 00:03:19.779
Even two decades after The Wind Waker's release,
it's absolutely gorgeous to look at.

00:03:19.779 --> 00:03:23.680
The Wind Waker may have suffered due to its
platform, but it still holds on as one of

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:27.090
the strongest entries in a consistently strong
series of games.

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:31.709
Luckily, an HD remaster was released later
on so a wider audience could play the game.

00:03:31.709 --> 00:03:34.449
Unfortunately, that platform was the Wii U.

00:03:35.449 --> 00:03:38.299
A phrase you often hear tossed around with
incredible games is that they "revolutionize

00:03:38.299 --> 00:03:39.299
the genre."

00:03:39.299 --> 00:03:43.420
A lot of games on this list could probably
claim they achieved this lofty goal, but Half-Life

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:45.269
might have the best claim to it.

00:03:45.269 --> 00:03:49.279
Many other genres have moved past their classic
roots, but shooters still get compared to

00:03:49.279 --> 00:03:52.989
Valve's darling, even though it was released
over two decades ago.

00:03:52.989 --> 00:03:57.870
Half-Life follows the voiceless protagonist
Gordon Freeman as he battles human and inter-dimensional

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:00.760
enemies through the Black Mesa research facility.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:05.469
It has been described as "the definitive single-player
game in a first-person shooter" and "the closest

00:04:05.469 --> 00:04:08.449
thing to a revolutionary step the genre has
ever taken."

00:04:09.449 --> 00:04:12.519
It's hard to believe that the fifth Elder
Scrolls title was released all the way back

00:04:12.519 --> 00:04:13.519
in 2011.

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:17.480
There have been so many different versions,
mods, rereleases, and ports that it would

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:20.350
be easy to guess the game "released" just
a few years ago.

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:24.470
It regularly sits in the top half of Steam's
player count lists, an impressive feat for

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:27.510
a decade-old game that has no multiplayer
to speak of.

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:32.410
Skyrim puts players into the role of the Dragonborn,
a legendary warrior with the ability to learn

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:34.280
powerful, magical abilities.

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:36.480
"Su'um ahrk morah.

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:41.880
You will push the world harder than it pushes
back."

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:46.560
More importantly than that, it gives aspiring
adventurers a playground to run wild in, flexing

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:50.930
their role-playing muscles and providing a
near limitless way to approach character building

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:51.950
and questing.

00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:55.100
The AV Club summed it up nicely in its review,
saying.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:58.880
"[Skyrim helps players] feel like the game
is happening to them, and they are alive in

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:02.030
it—not just cogs in a pre-fab game experience.

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:04.840
That's what sets Skyrim apart from some of
its contemporaries."

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:08.950
You could argue that this is a concept that
every open world game sets out to achieve,

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:10.130
but few truly do.

00:05:11.130 --> 00:05:14.380
One of the last major releases for the GameCube
was one of its most beloved.

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:18.780
The Legend of Zelda: Twilight Princess also
released as a launch title for the Wii, and

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:22.940
both versions have fans who swear "their"
version of the game is the superior one.

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:27.010
Twilight Princess saw Link attempting to save
Hyrule from becoming overtaken by another

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:29.140
dimension called the Twilight Realm.

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:33.270
The player could shift back and forth between
the two dimensions, and Link could also transform

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:35.840
into a powerful wolf for a host of new abilities.

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:38.460
The Legend of Zelda games tend to land in
one of two camps.

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:42.500
They are either experimental in many of their
design choices, or they attempt to perfect

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:44.200
elements of past games.

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:46.890
Twilight Princess may fall into that latter
category.

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:51.520
It's lauded for its dark, engrossing story
and cinematic style, and is often compared

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:54.490
to other heavy-hitters in the franchise like
Ocarina of Time.

00:05:54.490 --> 00:05:58.800
It may not have taken many big risks, but
it absolutely nailed what it set out to do.

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:03.950
The Mass Effect series is frequently heralded
as a tremendous bit of modern gaming, and

00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:08.910
almost any fan of BioWare's space opera RPG
will tell you that Mass Effect 2 is the best

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:10.390
entry in the series.

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:14.070
You could probably make a strong argument
that the reason Mass Effect 3 released to

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:18.710
such a negative response was because the second
game set the bar far too high.

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:22.740
A lot of story-driven games get knocked because
your decisions ultimately don't affect the

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:24.930
outcome beyond the surface level.

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:27.480
That is absolutely not the case in Mass Effect
2.

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:31.430
The choices you make, the quests you go on
throughout the game's extended runtime, the

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:35.870
way you play, and the strategic options you
choose in the game's climax can all have huge

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:38.330
repercussions on the way things play out.

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:42.310
It's fascinating reading about the different
endings people see and which crew members

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:44.990
don't make it out of the final mission alive.

00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:49.170
Few games truly give you that level of ownership,
and it's hard to think of any that do it as

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:50.600
well as Mass Effect 2.

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:55.580
The intricacies and mechanics of every fighting
game take a massive amount of skill and hours

00:06:55.580 --> 00:06:57.280
of practice to crack.

00:06:57.280 --> 00:07:01.860
While games like Street Fighter, Mortal Kombat,
Super Smash Bros. , and more all have pro

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:06.960
scenes and complex webs of mechanics to master,
few major fighting franchises are as complex

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:11.960
as Tekken, and few games are as revered in
their franchises as Tekken 3.

00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:16.700
Like any fighting game worth its salt, Tekken
3 had an absolutely bananas storyline involving

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:21.371
demons, corporations, and, of course, a fighting
tournament that determines the fate of the

00:07:21.371 --> 00:07:22.371
world.

00:07:22.371 --> 00:07:26.080
More importantly, it has a diverse cast of
balanced characters to go along with a deep

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:28.770
and impressive combo system and move list.

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:30.460
It also looks and feels great.

00:07:30.460 --> 00:07:34.639
Tekken 2 was a masterpiece as well, and the
second and third entries are still considered

00:07:34.639 --> 00:07:36.810
the best the series ever put on offer.

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:41.530
Many reviewers felt that the complete console
version of Tekken 3 is actually a better experience

00:07:41.530 --> 00:07:42.560
than its arcade counterpart.

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:47.930
The Arkham franchise helped redefine open
world action games and created what many think

00:07:47.930 --> 00:07:51.700
of as one of the best superhero games of all
time in the process.

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:55.810
Even Arkham's less-than-stellar efforts were
a lot of fun to play, but many would argue

00:07:55.810 --> 00:08:00.010
that Batman: Arkham City is the crowning achievement
of the franchise.

00:08:00.010 --> 00:08:04.210
Arkham City allowed gamers to truly immerse
themselves in the role of the Dark Knight.

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:08.710
The rush from swinging among familiar Gotham
City landmarks, beating down dozens of foes

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:13.290
at once with elaborate, but simple to perform,
combos, and taking on a colorful rogue's gallery

00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:14.790
was all part of the fun.

00:08:14.790 --> 00:08:19.650
The big names like Joker, Penguin, Riddler,
and Mr. Freeze are all here, alongside deeper

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:22.860
cuts like Solomon Grundy and Victor Zsasz.

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:27.180
Reviewers called Batman: Arkham City the best
licensed video game ever made, and nearly

00:08:27.180 --> 00:08:31.790
every review commended it for one-upping its
already beloved predecessor, Arkham Asylum,

00:08:31.790 --> 00:08:33.639
in almost every way.

00:08:34.639 --> 00:08:37.889
The Orange Box might just represent the greatest
collection of games ever put together.

00:08:37.889 --> 00:08:42.219
This incredible collection packed in five
games, and all are still held in fairly high

00:08:42.219 --> 00:08:43.219
regard.

00:08:43.219 --> 00:08:47.079
The original Half-Life was heralded as one
of the most important games of all time, and

00:08:47.079 --> 00:08:49.870
its sequel improved upon it in almost every
way.

00:08:49.870 --> 00:08:53.520
Half-Life 2 itself would have been part of
this list, but its inclusion in The Orange

00:08:53.520 --> 00:08:55.760
Box made that a little redundant.

00:08:55.760 --> 00:09:00.160
Half-Life 2: Episode One was included here
as a bridge to Episode Two, which was first

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:01.950
released as part of The Orange Box.

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:06.550
It's probably the weakest of the five included
games, though it is still pretty impressive.

00:09:06.550 --> 00:09:10.970
Half-Life 2: Episode Two served as the big
draw for many gamers with The Orange Box,

00:09:10.970 --> 00:09:13.699
seeing as this was how the episode debuted.

00:09:13.699 --> 00:09:17.160
Years and years later, fans are still clamoring
for Episode Three.

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:21.170
Team Fortress 2 was one of Valve's biggest
moneymakers, and continues to be one of the

00:09:21.170 --> 00:09:22.910
most popular shooters in the world.

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:25.290
Finally, Portal made it into the bundle.

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:29.399
What seemed like a throwaway tech demo actually
proved to be one of the most influential games

00:09:29.399 --> 00:09:30.399
of all time.

00:09:31.399 --> 00:09:35.079
Most gamers who were around in the GameCube
era have some memory of Resident Evil 4.

00:09:35.079 --> 00:09:39.120
The opening action scene, where Leon is attacked
by a group of villagers armed with farming

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:43.220
equipment, and one seriously pissed-off guy
with a chainsaw, is one of the most memorable

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:45.089
action scenes of all time.

00:09:45.089 --> 00:09:48.779
The Resident Evil series was well-loved but
a bit fiddly up until this point.

00:09:48.779 --> 00:09:50.699
"Jill, here's a lockpick.

00:09:50.699 --> 00:09:56.600
It might be handy if you, the Master of Unlocking,
take it with you."

00:09:56.600 --> 00:10:00.300
A lot of the tension in the original three
games derived from the tank-like controls

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:02.839
that made quick escapes almost impossible.

00:10:02.839 --> 00:10:06.999
Resident Evil 4 changed all that, veering
into more traditional control territory while

00:10:06.999 --> 00:10:09.879
still maintaining the tense and terrifying
atmosphere.

00:10:09.879 --> 00:10:14.640
The story is still nonsensical in a delightful
B-Movie way, but it all adds to the game's

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:15.640
charm.

00:10:15.640 --> 00:10:18.699
Reviewers often discussed how the game set
the benchmark for the series on its original

00:10:18.699 --> 00:10:19.940
release on the GameCube.

00:10:19.940 --> 00:10:24.249
A few elements are a bit wonky, but Resident
Evil 4 still holds up.

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:28.180
Uncharted 2: Among Thieves is one of the most
surprising entries on this list.

00:10:28.180 --> 00:10:32.010
Not because it isn't an incredible game, but
because it isn't typically a franchise that

00:10:32.010 --> 00:10:33.579
gets mentioned in the all-time greats.

00:10:33.579 --> 00:10:35.980
That suits the game's tone just fine.

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:40.129
A wild adventure with a compelling multiplayer
mode and plenty of opportunities to make your

00:10:40.129 --> 00:10:45.040
own carnage, Uncharted 2 is a near-perfect
adventure that really showcases what the best

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:46.810
video games can do.

00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:50.801
Reviewers often comment that the attention
to detail is beyond compare and that the game

00:10:50.801 --> 00:10:52.430
is an essential experience.

00:10:52.430 --> 00:10:55.930
PlayStation Universe said,
"[It's] quite possibly the best game to have

00:10:55.930 --> 00:11:00.449
graced the PS3, and without a doubt one of
the greatest titles ever conceived."

00:11:00.449 --> 00:11:04.850
Much of the attention surrounding Among Thieves
is that it just feels like an action movie.

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:07.100
It's cinematic, but you always feel in control.

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:11.699
It's a game that lets players live as Indiana
Jones and their other favorite adventurers,

00:11:11.699 --> 00:11:14.740
and that's reason enough to put it so high
on the all-time greats list.

00:11:15.740 --> 00:11:20.050
The Nintendo 64 has more than its fair share
of nostalgia bombs, but few hold a candle

00:11:20.050 --> 00:11:21.990
to GoldenEye 007.

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:25.559
Part of its hold on the collective gaming
consciousness has to do with the fact that

00:11:25.559 --> 00:11:30.130
some odd licensing disputes have made any
sort of rerelease or remaster of GoldenEye

00:11:30.130 --> 00:11:35.250
dead in the water, so the only way to play
it outside of ROMs is in its original Nintendo

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:36.250
64 form.

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:40.529
It can be easy to forget that one of the big
draws for the game at the time was the single-player

00:11:40.529 --> 00:11:41.529
mode.

00:11:41.529 --> 00:11:45.520
Licensed games were, and still are, often
seen as cash grabs, but GoldenEye did a great

00:11:45.520 --> 00:11:49.399
job of translating aspects of the film into
a fun and coherent game.

00:11:49.399 --> 00:11:52.720
What most people remember, however, is the
game's multiplayer.

00:11:52.720 --> 00:11:56.939
The four-person, split-screen experience ate
away the hours as players screen-sniped and

00:11:56.939 --> 00:11:58.769
golden-gunned one another.

00:11:58.769 --> 00:12:03.550
GoldenEye remains a masterpiece as both a
console shooter and a couch-multiplayer legend.

00:12:04.550 --> 00:12:08.290
In hindsight, BioShock seems like a surefire
hit, but the game was a pretty big risk at

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:09.290
the time.

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:14.240
An entirely original IP with a strange art
style, no multiplayer to speak of, and a cerebral

00:12:14.240 --> 00:12:17.709
storyline about ethics crammed into a first-person
shooter?

00:12:17.709 --> 00:12:18.959
It was no sure thing.

00:12:18.959 --> 00:12:23.800
Luckily, BioShock was beautifully put together
and planned, and its unique creative direction

00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:27.959
drew people in who were tired of outer space
and World War 2 shooters.

00:12:27.959 --> 00:12:32.939
Nearly every aspect of BioShock was praised
for pushing boundaries and perfect execution.

00:12:32.939 --> 00:12:36.920
Even if certain mechanics seem typical by
today’s standards, BioShock helped pave

00:12:36.920 --> 00:12:40.139
the way for elements like combat customization
and stealth.

00:12:40.139 --> 00:12:44.269
The story was also incredible, and the big
twist has become the stuff of legend.

00:12:44.269 --> 00:12:48.320
About the only knock against BioShock is the
final boss battle, something that even the

00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:51.240
game's designers have said was a mistake.

00:12:51.240 --> 00:12:54.610
"A man chooses.

00:12:54.610 --> 00:12:56.819
A slave obeys."

00:12:58.759 --> 00:13:03.399
Back in the day, the rivalry between the Madden
and 2K Football franchises was intense.

00:13:03.399 --> 00:13:08.519
Each side had supporters, with Madden often
coming out on top due to familiarity and market

00:13:08.519 --> 00:13:13.009
saturation, and eventually, completely knocking
its competitor out of the game.

00:13:13.009 --> 00:13:18.399
However, purists were often bigger fans of
2K, with NFL 2K1 often being highlighted as

00:13:18.399 --> 00:13:20.449
the franchise at its absolute best.

00:13:20.449 --> 00:13:26.470
2K1 improved on the previous year's also stellar
entry by introducing some major improvements.

00:13:26.470 --> 00:13:31.110
It included better animations and artificial
intelligence as well as totally revamping

00:13:31.110 --> 00:13:32.259
the running game.

00:13:32.259 --> 00:13:38.279
NFL 2K1 also introduced one of the most important
gaming features of all time: Online multiplayer.

00:13:38.279 --> 00:13:42.040
It was the first sports game that let you
find opponents online, something that's tough

00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:44.790
to imagine any competitive game going without
these days.

00:13:45.790 --> 00:13:50.350
The Xbox had powerful specs when it hit the
scene in November 2001, but it needed something

00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:54.999
extra to make a mark against the vast catalog
of games in Sony and Nintendo's stables.

00:13:54.999 --> 00:13:57.749
It had just the thing in Halo: Combat Evolved.

00:13:57.749 --> 00:14:02.480
Halo was a sci-fi shooter that captured so
many of the best elements of the games before

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:03.480
it.

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:07.910
It featured an incredible single-player campaign
full of cinematic missions and an epic storyline.

00:14:07.910 --> 00:14:12.589
It had memorable characters and graphics that
made it stand out as a must-see video game.

00:14:12.589 --> 00:14:17.550
On top of all that, it had near limitless
gameplay due to its intense multiplayer options,

00:14:17.550 --> 00:14:22.069
giving players all sorts of ways to have late
night frag sessions and white-knuckle competitive

00:14:22.069 --> 00:14:23.069
matches.

00:14:23.069 --> 00:14:27.069
It's not hyperbolic to suggest that Microsoft's
console foray may not have found its footing

00:14:27.069 --> 00:14:28.579
if it weren't for Halo: Combat Evolved.

00:14:29.579 --> 00:14:32.509
It's about time the world's most famous plumber
made the list.

00:14:32.509 --> 00:14:36.499
And you could probably pick from about a dozen
entries in this incredibly long-lived series

00:14:36.499 --> 00:14:39.009
as the "best" and make a compelling case.

00:14:39.009 --> 00:14:43.310
Super Mario Odyssey for the Nintendo Switch
towers above them all, making perfect use

00:14:43.310 --> 00:14:47.230
of the hardware to combine all the best aspects
of past Mario games.

00:14:47.230 --> 00:14:50.149
If you've got a Switch and haven't played
it, you're missing out.

00:14:50.149 --> 00:14:54.360
Super Mario Odyssey's central sticking point
is Cappy, a sentient piece of headwear that

00:14:54.360 --> 00:14:59.110
gives Mario the ability to take control of
enemies and use their special abilities.

00:14:59.110 --> 00:15:03.839
This capability makes for a seemingly infinite
number of fun and hilarious combinations to

00:15:03.839 --> 00:15:08.350
solve the game's puzzles, and it's extremely
easy to just get lost in messing around with

00:15:08.350 --> 00:15:10.670
the different abilities at your disposal.

00:15:10.670 --> 00:15:15.480
Super Mario Odyssey captures something magical
that the best Nintendo games typically do.

00:15:15.480 --> 00:15:18.970
Reviews called it one of Nintendo's greatest
gaming achievements ever.

00:15:18.970 --> 00:15:21.519
That's some pretty high praise for the legendary
studio.

00:15:22.519 --> 00:15:26.580
It's a shame the GameCube didn't sell better,
as it housed a few incredible games during

00:15:26.580 --> 00:15:27.580
its lifespan.

00:15:27.580 --> 00:15:31.850
About a year after the console's original
release, it saw one of its best ever, and

00:15:31.850 --> 00:15:35.779
a welcome return to form for a Nintendo legend:
Metroid Prime.

00:15:35.779 --> 00:15:39.920
Metroid Prime showed that the legendary Samus
could do a first-person shooter just as well

00:15:39.920 --> 00:15:43.949
as she could do a side-scrolling platformer,
and marked the first game in the series in

00:15:43.949 --> 00:15:45.369
nearly a decade.

00:15:45.369 --> 00:15:49.259
Metroid Prime didn't miss a beat though, and
helped showcase just how powerful the GameCube

00:15:49.259 --> 00:15:53.579
hardware was with its impressive visuals and
expansive world to explore.

00:15:53.579 --> 00:15:57.990
Metroid Prime is praised on almost every level
for its design, mechanics, and storytelling.

00:15:57.990 --> 00:16:00.449
It’s been called a must-have masterpiece.

00:16:00.449 --> 00:16:04.389
Fans have seen other Metroid games since,
but few have reached the highs the first Metroid

00:16:04.389 --> 00:16:06.439
Prime maintained throughout its playtime.

00:16:07.439 --> 00:16:11.920
GoldenEye was a tough game to follow up, but
Rare outdid itself with its spiritual successor,

00:16:11.920 --> 00:16:12.920
Perfect Dark.

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:15.989
Anyone who spent hours in the world of James
Bond would feel right at home in the world

00:16:15.989 --> 00:16:20.559
of Joanna Dark, and the additions it made
to the already great existing formula helped

00:16:20.559 --> 00:16:25.119
solidify Perfect Dark as one of the Nintendo
64's crowning achievements.

00:16:25.119 --> 00:16:29.540
There is just so much good in Perfect Dark
that it's tough to focus on specific elements.

00:16:29.540 --> 00:16:34.240
GoldenEye's multiplayer came back better than
ever, with a huge array of weapons and modes,

00:16:34.240 --> 00:16:37.610
ingenious level design, and even AI-controlled
bots.

00:16:37.610 --> 00:16:42.009
The single-player story weaved a cheesy and
engrossing sci-fi yarn, complete with an alien

00:16:42.009 --> 00:16:43.110
buddy named Elvis.

00:16:43.110 --> 00:16:44.110
"What's wrong?"

00:16:44.110 --> 00:16:46.110
"I have a headache.

00:16:46.110 --> 00:16:50.619
And with a head this big, that's no joke."

00:16:50.619 --> 00:16:54.980
Almost every review of Perfect Dark features
some variation of "Like GoldenEye, but better

00:16:54.980 --> 00:16:56.379
in every way."

00:16:56.379 --> 00:16:59.049
That's certainly praise enough to land it
on the list of all-time greats.

00:17:00.329 --> 00:17:04.199
There are a substantial number of games from
The Legend of Zelda series that are considered

00:17:04.199 --> 00:17:06.300
"near perfect," and the latest is no exception.

00:17:06.300 --> 00:17:10.589
After Nintendo squandered a bit of its goodwill
towards gamers with the confusing marketing

00:17:10.589 --> 00:17:14.810
approach to the Wii U, the Nintendo Switch
was the company's chance to get back in the

00:17:14.810 --> 00:17:15.810
game.

00:17:15.810 --> 00:17:19.400
Luckily, there was a launch day game worthy
of some hype: The absolutely breathtaking

00:17:19.400 --> 00:17:21.960
The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild.

00:17:21.960 --> 00:17:25.571
Reviews praised Breath of the Wild for nailing
mechanics from other open world games, but

00:17:25.571 --> 00:17:28.160
also being willing to experiment and take
chances.

00:17:28.160 --> 00:17:32.840
It really is unlike any other game in the
franchise before it, and most of the criticisms

00:17:32.840 --> 00:17:34.650
of the game are minimal and nitpicky.

00:17:34.650 --> 00:17:38.410
Breath of the Wild is one of those games that
everyone who owns a Nintendo Switch should

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:39.410
have a go at.

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:43.930
Nintendo has often taken some bold leaps in
introducing new mechanics to its flagship

00:17:43.930 --> 00:17:47.540
properties, and Super Mario Galaxy was one
of its biggest yet.

00:17:47.540 --> 00:17:52.520
It essentially took the formula set by Super
Mario 64 and perfected it for the motion control

00:17:52.520 --> 00:17:53.620
scheme of the Wii.

00:17:53.620 --> 00:17:58.190
The game still stands as one of the most innovative
and best uses of the console's hardware ever

00:17:58.190 --> 00:17:59.240
released.

00:17:59.240 --> 00:18:01.740
Super Mario Galaxy just presses all the right
buttons.

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:04.720
It's a game that Destructoid gushed over by
saying:

00:18:04.720 --> 00:18:08.520
"This is the first game on the Wii that I
can recommend without hesitation to gamers

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:12.310
of any stock, from any background — a truly
must-own title.

00:18:12.310 --> 00:18:17.460
[It] improves upon flaws in Mario 64 that
I hadn't even noticed until…Galaxy did it

00:18:17.460 --> 00:18:18.460
better."

00:18:18.460 --> 00:18:21.820
If you're lucky enough to have a Wii or Wii
U sitting around, or if you managed to grab

00:18:21.820 --> 00:18:26.390
Super Mario 3D All-Stars for Switch before
it disappeared, this is definitely a game

00:18:26.390 --> 00:18:27.390
you should play.

00:18:28.390 --> 00:18:31.460
Ever since the series was reinvented with
its third installment, the Grand Theft Auto

00:18:31.460 --> 00:18:34.780
franchise has reigned as one of the most popular
in all of gaming.

00:18:34.780 --> 00:18:39.010
The most recent release, Grand Theft Auto
5, executes almost everything the series is

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:40.530
known for perfectly.

00:18:40.530 --> 00:18:44.400
It's equal parts crime simulator, life simulator,
and incredible tech demo.

00:18:44.400 --> 00:18:49.860
At the time of its release, IGN said of GTA5:
"It represents a refinement of everything

00:18:49.860 --> 00:18:53.010
that GTA IV brought to the table five years
ago.

00:18:53.010 --> 00:18:57.200
It's technically more accomplished in every
conceivable way, but it's also tremendously

00:18:57.200 --> 00:18:59.000
ambitious in its own right."

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:03.190
The three-pronged approach to the story, featuring
wildly different protagonists, incredible

00:19:03.190 --> 00:19:07.200
attention to detail, and the sheer amount
of stuff hidden in the world make it hard

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:10.200
to load up GTA5 and not get a smile on your
face.

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:14.390
"We might have to chop you up into little
pieces before spraying your pulp mess down

00:19:14.390 --> 00:19:17.940
the drain, but I really hope it doesn't come
to that."

00:19:18.940 --> 00:19:22.850
The release of Red Dead Redemption 2 was one
of the most anticipated game releases of recent

00:19:22.850 --> 00:19:26.480
memory, and a lot of people weren't sure it
could live up to the hype and high bar set

00:19:26.480 --> 00:19:28.350
by the previous title.

00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:32.910
Rockstar Games delivered far above most players'
expectations, with one of the best examples

00:19:32.910 --> 00:19:35.370
of open world gameplay seen to date.

00:19:35.370 --> 00:19:39.650
Like Rockstar's other big series, part of
what makes Red Dead Redemption 2 so incredible

00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:41.450
is how alive the world feels.

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:45.240
Riding your horse through the wilderness,
it seems like you're just a tiny part of a

00:19:45.240 --> 00:19:49.050
living, breathing universe and that you might
stumble across something new at any moment.

00:19:49.050 --> 00:19:53.230
It's one of those games that is greater than
the sum of its parts, and truly stands as

00:19:53.230 --> 00:19:55.980
an "experience" that everyone interested in
gaming should have.

00:19:56.990 --> 00:20:01.430
Until Super Mario Galaxy 2 debuted, Nintendo
hadn’t released a direct sequel to a Super

00:20:01.430 --> 00:20:03.820
Mario game in almost twenty years.

00:20:03.820 --> 00:20:07.740
It speaks to how frequently Nintendo tries
to stretch the boundaries with its red-capped

00:20:07.740 --> 00:20:12.650
mascot, and it also shows just how imaginative
the original Super Mario Galaxy was.

00:20:12.650 --> 00:20:15.710
It contained enough new ideas to spawn a follow-up.

00:20:15.710 --> 00:20:21.020
Super Mario Galaxy 2 isn't particularly innovative,
but it's another of those "just plain fun"

00:20:21.020 --> 00:20:23.900
games where you can't really describe what
makes it so good.

00:20:23.900 --> 00:20:28.380
It takes the already impressive gameplay of
the previous game and makes it even better.

00:20:29.380 --> 00:20:33.040
Despite the popularity of franchises like
Street Fighter and Tekken, the highest-rated

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:37.600
fighting game on Metacritic actually comes
from a different franchise: SoulCalibur.

00:20:37.600 --> 00:20:41.340
Though SoulCalibur is not the original game
in the franchise, that would be Soul Edge,

00:20:41.340 --> 00:20:44.990
it was the first to get a major release and
was one of the heaviest hitters in the early

00:20:44.990 --> 00:20:46.920
lineup of the Sega Dreamcast.

00:20:46.920 --> 00:20:51.800
The franchise has had some strong releases
since this game hit the Dreamcast in 1999,

00:20:51.800 --> 00:20:53.690
but none have been quite so impactful.

00:20:53.690 --> 00:20:57.860
It truly showcased the Dreamcast's hardware
in a magnificent way, as nearly every review

00:20:57.860 --> 00:21:00.570
of the game touched on how incredible it looked
at the time.

00:21:00.570 --> 00:21:04.940
It was largely seen as the best reason to
own a Sega Dreamcast, and continues to hold

00:21:04.940 --> 00:21:08.700
up as one of the finest examples of a 3D fighter
ever released.

00:21:10.190 --> 00:21:13.020
Grand Theft Auto 4 could probably stake a
claim as one of the most influential games

00:21:13.020 --> 00:21:14.230
of all time.

00:21:14.230 --> 00:21:18.370
Returning to Liberty City in GTA4 was, quite
literally, a whole new world.

00:21:18.370 --> 00:21:23.280
Every NPC seemingly had an agenda, and there
is such a huge variety of things to do that

00:21:23.280 --> 00:21:28.030
you could put hundreds of hours into GTA4
and still discover new things along the way.

00:21:28.030 --> 00:21:32.120
On top of all that, it implemented several
multiplayer modes that, while not quite as

00:21:32.120 --> 00:21:37.200
extensive as what's now seen in GTA Online,
surely paved the way for what the series would

00:21:37.200 --> 00:21:38.200
become.

00:21:38.200 --> 00:21:45.040
"War is where the young and stupid are tricked
by the old and bitter into killing each other."

00:21:45.040 --> 00:21:49.930
GameSpot's review of GTA4 summed it up nicely:
"Grand Theft Auto IV is a game that you simply

00:21:49.930 --> 00:21:50.930
have to play."

00:21:51.930 --> 00:21:56.120
There is a certain subset of gamers who, when
reading anything about the Tony Hawk Pro Skater

00:21:56.120 --> 00:21:58.850
franchise, will immediately start humming
or singing.

00:21:58.850 --> 00:22:03.530
Chances are, that song comes from the soundtrack
of Tony Hawk's Pro Skater 2, universally viewed

00:22:03.530 --> 00:22:05.270
as the high point of the series.

00:22:05.270 --> 00:22:09.660
The first Pro Skater game laid the groundwork
and capitalized on the rising popularity of

00:22:09.660 --> 00:22:13.910
extreme sports to make for a memorable romp
through some wild skate parks.

00:22:13.910 --> 00:22:17.700
However, Tony Hawk's Pro Skater 2 raised the
bar by a huge margin.

00:22:17.700 --> 00:22:20.990
It’s the highest rated game ever released
for the PlayStation.

00:22:20.990 --> 00:22:24.850
Which is an incredible feat when you remember
just how many revolutionary games came out

00:22:24.850 --> 00:22:25.850
for the console.

00:22:26.850 --> 00:22:31.210
Metacritic's records go back over two decades,
and tens of thousands of video game reviews

00:22:31.210 --> 00:22:33.090
run through its ranking system.

00:22:33.090 --> 00:22:37.690
Only one game on the entire website has a
99 rating: The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of

00:22:37.690 --> 00:22:38.690
Time.

00:22:38.690 --> 00:22:43.500
The Nintendo 64 was home to several reinventions
of classic franchises, but Ocarina of Time

00:22:43.500 --> 00:22:47.340
stands out as the true masterpiece of N64's
library.

00:22:47.340 --> 00:22:51.620
The hype surrounding Ocarina of Time, or "Zelda
64" as it was often called, was immense.

00:22:51.620 --> 00:22:56.130
And yet, somehow, it delivered and exceeded
almost everything gamers were hoping for.

00:22:56.130 --> 00:22:59.180
In the IGN review for Ocarina of Time, the
site wrote:

00:22:59.180 --> 00:23:05.240
"When the final version of Zelda 64 arrived
in the IGN64 offices, we stopped working,

00:23:05.240 --> 00:23:10.870
locked ourselves into a room with a big-screen
TV and a surround system and played 17 hours

00:23:10.870 --> 00:23:11.870
straight.

00:23:11.870 --> 00:23:15.230
After only a few hours of sleep, we were back
for more and we couldn't stop until we finished

00:23:15.230 --> 00:23:16.230
the game.

00:23:16.230 --> 00:23:18.960
Then, we started over again to find all the
secrets."

00:23:18.960 --> 00:23:23.510
There is almost no fault to be found in Ocarina
of Time, and it sets an incredibly high bar

00:23:23.510 --> 00:23:25.230
for the genre to this day.

00:23:25.230 --> 00:23:28.420
It's practically perfect, and thus stands
alone atop the list.

